# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (used by the `tsan` test preset).
#
# SQLite's WAL index lives in a memory-mapped -shm file shared by every connection. Readers
# (walIndexTryHdr) read the header without a lock, twice, and accept it only if both copies and the
# checksum agree; the writer (walIndexWriteHdr) publishes it under the WAL write lock. That lock-free
# retry protocol is intentional and is synchronised by fcntl locks and memory barriers that
# ThreadSanitizer cannot model, so it reports a "race" between two connections of the same process.
# Only SQLite's WAL-index routines are listed; races in Loom code are not affected.
race:walIndexTryHdr
race:walIndexWriteHdr
race:walIndexReadHdr
race:walIndexAppend
race:walIndexRecover
race:walCheckpoint
race:walTryBeginRead
race:walRestartHdr
race:walRestartLog
race:sqlite3WalFrames
# unixOpen resets the PRNG when the pid changed; SQLite documents that concurrent resets "are harmless".
race:unixOpen
